<title>JAPAN: Chuo Trust (Trust Account) reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Chuo Trust (Trust Account) reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chuo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Mar 97     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans		5.4	     27.0</p>
<p>  Bad loans			   9.8	     16.6</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	   37.3	     60.0</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    52.5	    103.6</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more.</p>
</text>
